Design a circuit that operates as an 8-bit data swapper. This module takes an 8-bit input and rearranges its bits such that the upper 4 bits are swapped with the lower 4 bits. Specifically, when the input bits are labeled from 0 to 7, the output will reflect the bits in the following order: the original bit 4 becomes bit 0, bit 5 becomes bit 1, bit 6 becomes bit 2, bit 7 becomes bit 3, and conversely, bit 0 becomes bit 4, bit 1 becomes bit 5, bit 2 becomes bit 6, and bit 3 becomes bit 7.
