Design a circuit that captures a 4-bit shift register and counts the number of zeros in the least significant bit over a series of clock cycles. The circuit takes a 127-bit input signal, shifting in the most significant bit while maintaining a 4-bit history in the shift register. The output is a 7-bit wide register reflecting the count of zeros detected.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [126:0] in,
    output reg [6:0] out
);

